  "body": "Hi,\n\nThere seems to be a little quirk in ART, regarding how ratings are displayed when they are stored in XMP files: I used to use Adobe CS 6 together with Bridge, to sort, rate and edit my photos. I now use ART exclusively for that. Sometimes I go back to old folders to review what I had, and I noticed that photos that I have rejected are shown as 5 stars and as being rejected in ART (stars + trashcan) . This does not happen with XMP files that were created with ART.\n\nIt's no big issue, but it's kind of weird. I'd happily provide examples of \"offending\" XMP files.\n\nThanks for your time and work!\nRobert",
